  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.8,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["R1", "R8"],
      "pins": ["J8.3", "J9.3", "U2.6"],
      "nets": ["Net-(J8-Pin_3)", "Net-(J9-Pin_3)", "/NET0009"],
      "observed": "R1 (0Ω) directly bridges J8 pin 3 and J9 pin 3, and R8 (0Ω) connects J9 pin 3 to U2 pin 6 (A). These jumpers are populated in the schematic, permanently tying the two servo signal pins together and to the MAX3485 A line.",
      "expected": "The specification states R13/R14 are 0Ω jumpers that are populated only for serial mode; in PWM mode they must be left open so each servo header has an independent PWM signal. The netlist shows them as present 0Ω components, which would short the two PWM channels together if the board is built as shown.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R13, R14 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | When shorted, bridge J3-pin3 and J8-pin3 together and onto the MAX3485 TTL bus — schematic note: \"Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo\"."},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R1\") (value \"0\") ... (comp (ref \"R8\") (value \"0\") ... (net (code \"35\") (name \"Net-(J8-Pin_3)\") (node (ref \"J8\") (pin \"3\") ... (node (ref \"R1\") (pin \"2\") ... (net (code \"36\") (name \"Net-(J9-Pin_3)\") (node (ref \"J9\") (pin \"3\") ... (node (ref \"R1\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\") ... (net (code \"9\") (name \"/NET0009\") (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"1\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"6\") ..."}
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled with R1 and R8 populated (as the netlist implies), the two servo signal lines are shorted together and to the RS-485 A line, preventing independent PWM control and potentially damaging the MAX3485 if PWM signals are driven simultaneously.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show the serial-mode jumpers R1 and R8 as 0Ω components that permanently bridge the two servo signal pins and connect them to the MAX3485 A line, which contradicts the specification's requirement that these jumpers be open for PWM mode and only populated for serial mode."
}

